        <item>
            <title>0.9</title>
            <pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 07:10:27 -0700</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>837</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.9</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>26.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <sparkle:hardwareRequirements>arm64</sparkle:hardwareRequirements>
            <description><![CDATA[<style>
:root { color-scheme: light dark; }
body { font-family: -apple-system, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 13px; color: #1a1a1a; margin: 12px; }
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) { body { color: #e6e6e6; } }
h2 { font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 8px; } ul { margin: 4px 0 10px; padding-left: 20px; } li { margin-bottom: 3px; }
</style>
<h2>Asobi 0.9 (build 837)</h2>
<ul>
<li>The <b>Session</b> menu is now <b>Share</b>, and says what each item is for: <b>Share This Review&#8230;</b> (&#8679;&#8984;R), <b>Review Manager&#8230;</b>, <b>Open Invite File&#8230;</b>, then <b>Make an Invite File for Asobi Review&#8230;</b> and <b>Issue an Asobi Review License&#8230;</b> for the studio, and <b>Leave This Review</b> for guests. The right-click menu carries the same list; File &#9656; Share to Web&#8230; is now <b>Share This Review to the Web&#8230;</b>. Nothing moved out of reach.</li>
<li>Plain words throughout the Share This Review window and the Review Manager: the review is <i>live</i> with <i>people</i> in it, connections are <i>over the internet</i> or <i>on this network</i>, the browser plays a <i>review copy</i>, one <i>passphrase</i> everywhere (no more &#8220;passcode&#8221;). The window&#8217;s progress line reads like a sentence (&#8220;Preparing the web link (2 of 3 clips)&#8230;&#8221;, &#8220;Live&#8221;) instead of an engine report.</li>
<li>Buttons say what they do: <b>Start Review</b>, <b>Join</b>, <b>Leave</b>, <b>Remove</b> (a person from the review), <b>Forget Browsers</b>, <b>Reconnect</b>, <b>Reopen</b>, <b>Withdraw Delivery</b>; the checkbox is <b>Only these people can join</b>.</li>
<li>The manual&#8217;s three books use the new names.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
